{
  "id": "ALAS2023-2026-3444",
  "title": "Amazon Linux 2023 - ALAS2023-2026-3444: Important priority package update for xorg-x11-server",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-11-12 09:00:00"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-11-12 09:00:00"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "Package updates are available for Amazon Linux 2023 that fix the following vulnerabilities:\nCVE-2026-109903:\n\tA flaw in the X.Org Server's XvQueryImageAttributes reply handling can result in clients receiving an incorrect data size value, potentially leading to improper buffer allocation or usage.\n\nCVE-2026-109096:\n\tA flaw in the X.Org Server's XvPutImage length validation can allow requests with missing image data to be processed, potentially leading to server crashes or misbehavior.\n\nCVE-2026-109095:\n\tAn integer overflow flaw in the X.Org Server's glamor Xv image size computation can result in out-of-bounds reads, potentially leading to server crashes or unintended memory access.\n\nCVE-2026-109093:\n\tA flaw in the X.Org Server's XTestFakeInput handling can result in a stack out-of-bounds write, potentially leading to server crashes or stack memory corruption.\n\nCVE-2026-109092:\n\tA bounds-checking flaw in the X.Org Server's XvShmPutImage handling can result in an out-of-bounds read or write, potentially leading to server crashes or memory corruption.\n\nCVE-2026-109091:\n\tA flaw in the X.Org Server's handling of EDID Display-Range descriptors can result in an out-of-bounds write, potentially leading to server crashes or memory corruption.\n",
